# Terms of use of the {{ rec.short }} digital platform

**Version {{ doc.version }}**

## 1. Who provides the service

{% filter wordwrap(88) %}
The digital platform of the energy community is provided by **{{ rec.name }}**. It covers the online membership application, the community app{{ ', the AI assistant' if features.ai_assistant else '' }} and notifications.
{%- endfilter +%}

- Address: {{ rec.registered_office }}, {{ rec.country.en }}.
- Tax code and VAT: {{ rec.tax_code }}.
- Email: {{ rec.email }}.
- PEC: {{ rec.pec }}.

**{{ platform.name }}** operates the platform on {{ rec.short }}'s behalf.

The platform is developed in the {{ project.name }} research project, funded by the European Union
under the {{ project.programme }} programme (grant agreement No. {{ project.grant_agreement }}).

## 2. What these terms are

These terms govern the use of the platform. They do not replace or amend:

- {{ rec.short }}'s statute;
- the energy community's rules;
- the resolutions of its governing bodies.

Those continue to govern your relationship with the cooperative, and they prevail in
case of conflict.

The platform's privacy notice describes how your data is processed.

## 3. Who can use the platform

- **The membership application** is open to anyone who wishes to become a member of
  {{ rec.short }}.
- **The community app** is for admitted members only.
  - Access is personal. Do not share your credentials.
  - Tell {{ rec.short }} if you think someone else has used them.
- If you use the platform on behalf of a business or an organisation, you confirm that
  you are authorised to do so.

## 4. What it offers

The app lets you:

- see the consumption and production of the meters and devices registered to you;
- see forecasts, estimates and suggestions for shifting consumption;
- take on commitments to suggestions, and collect points and badges;
- receive notifications;
{% if features.ai_assistant %}
- use the AI assistant;
{% endif %}
{% if features.dso_data_exchange %}
- decide on the sharing of your meter readings;
{% endif %}
- send feedback.

Features may change during the project. {{ rec.short }} announces relevant changes in the
app.

## 5. Forecasts, estimates and suggestions

- **Information only:** forecasts, estimates and suggestions are for information.
- **The incentive estimate** does not replace GSE's official calculation. What you are
  entitled to is determined by the community's statute and rules.
- **Suggestions** are optional. Following them or not has no consequence for your
  membership.
- **Points and badges** are a way to take part in community life. They have no monetary
  value, unless the community rules or a resolution provide otherwise.

{% set skip = 0 if features.ai_assistant else 1 %}
{% if features.ai_assistant %}
## 6. The AI assistant

- **What it is:** an **artificial intelligence system**. It answers using your data on
  the platform, with your own permissions.
- **Its answers can be wrong or incomplete.** They are not technical, legal, tax or
  financial advice. Check important information with {{ rec.short }}.
- **Do not attach** identity documents, health data or other people's personal data.
- You can delete your conversations and attachments at any time.

{% endif %}
## {{ 7 - skip }}. Proper use

When you use the platform, you agree:

- to give true and up-to-date information;
- not to access other members' data, and not to try to get around the platform's
  protections;
- not to use the platform{{ ', including the assistant,' if features.ai_assistant else '' }} for unlawful or offensive purposes,
  or for purposes unrelated to the community;
- not to upload content that infringes the rights of others;
- not to interfere with the platform's operation, for example through unauthorised
  automated access.

## {{ 8 - skip }}. Availability

- **Effort, not a guarantee:** the platform is developed and improved within a research
  project. {{ rec.short }} endeavours to keep it available and secure, but cannot guarantee
  that it always works without interruption or error.
- **Maintenance:** planned maintenance is announced in the app where possible.
- **Data delays:** the data shown may be delayed or incomplete, for example while the
  grid operator has not yet made it available.

## {{ 9 - skip }}. Suspension and termination

- You can stop using the app at any time.
- Your account is deactivated when your membership ends.
- {{ rec.short }} may suspend access for a serious breach of these terms, or to protect the
  platform's security. It tells you why, unless the law prevents it.
- After termination, your data is handled as described in the platform's privacy notice.

## {{ 10 - skip }}. Intellectual property

- **Software:** the platform's software is distributed by the {{ project.name }} project under open
  source licences, stated in the respective repositories.
- **Your content:** what you enter, such as messages and feedback, remains yours. You
  grant {{ rec.short }} the use needed to provide the service to you.

## {{ 11 - skip }}. Liability

- {{ rec.short }} is liable for damage caused wilfully or through gross negligence, and for
  any other liability that the law does not allow to be excluded.
- To the extent the law allows, {{ rec.short }} is not liable for decisions taken solely on
  the basis of {{ 'forecasts, estimates, suggestions or answers from the assistant' if features.ai_assistant else 'forecasts, estimates or suggestions' }}.
- If you are a consumer, your rights under the Italian Consumer Code are unaffected.

## {{ 12 - skip }}. Changes

- {{ rec.short }} may change these terms because of changes to the service, the law or the
  project.
- The new version is shown to you at your next login, and applies from when you accept
  it.
- If you do not accept it, you can stop using the app. Your membership is not affected.

## {{ 13 - skip }}. Governing law and disputes

- **Law:** these terms are governed by Italian law.
- **Conciliation:** disputes between {{ rec.short }} and its members are subject to the
  conciliation clause of the statute.
- **Court:** if you are a consumer, the court of the place where you live has
  jurisdiction.

